figdown 0.1 block
# `MARKER-TARGET-KINDS`: case 810's document, UNCHANGED, under the OLDEST header.
# The widening that lets `in=` resolve a region id is deliberately UNGATED,
# and this file is the assertion — the directive lines below are
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to case 810's and the header is the only difference.
#
# The pair 810/811 is the exact counterpart of the pair 805/806, and it comes
# out the OTHER WAY ROUND. 805/806 say `note=` is legal at 0.3 and refused
# below it; 810/811 say the region resolver behaves identically at 0.1 and at
# 0.3. Both changes shipped in the same release, so a reader who saw only one
# pair would take away a rule the project does not have — that 0.3
# gated everything it added, or that it gated nothing.
#
# The discriminator, argued at length in case 810: `note=` ADDS A SPELLING
# with a prior meaning on the record, and accepting it under an old header
# would repaint a tooltip as ink. This adds NO spelling — the core §10
# registry is byte-unchanged — and the only documents it affects are ones
# that previously did not parse at all. A widening with nothing to drift from
# does not need a version to hide behind.
#
# Keep the two bodies edited together; if a line moves in 810, move it here.
group pool "Resource pool"
node q0 "Q0" in=pool
table q "Queue depth"
| Slot | Depth |
|------|-------|
| s0 | 12 |
| s1 | 30 |
threshold "Max" in=q offset=50%
band "Reserved" 15..35% in=q
bitfield hdr "Header" word=32 numbering=msb0
field "Type" 8
field "Rest" 24
threshold "Split" in=hdr offset=25%
threshold "Group target, unchanged" in=pool offset=80%
threshold "Node target, unchanged" in=q0 offset=35%
